I go to the checkout.
The queue is fortunately shorter than before.
Soon it is my turn.
The cashier greets me warmly.
"Hello, did you find everything?" she asks.
"Yes, thank you," I answer.
I lay the green jacket and the yellow T-shirt on the counter.
She scans the clothes.
"That is ninety-five Euro, please," she says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the receipt?" she asks.
"Yes, please," I say.
I definitely need it.
Maybe I have to exchange the T-shirt.
She gives me the receipt.
"Thank you very much and have a nice weekend!" she says.
"Thanks, you too!" I reply.
Then I pack my new things neatly into my backpack.
I ride home.
I want to try everything on properly.
